/E (5. The 4 requirements above all relate to characteristics of high demand. The 5th requirement relates to supply. The float is a term used to describe the number of shares available to trade. When a company makes its Initial Public Offering \(IPO\) they sell a fixed number of shares onto the market. From that point forward, those shares are known as the float, and they represent the supply. Companies with less supply will tend to experience more dramatic imbalances between)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
